# Ceraa secrets template — copy to a non-tracked location and fill in.
# Used by ceraa.service (EnvironmentFile=/etc/ceraa/ceraa.env)
# and by run-ceraa.sh / start-bot.sh / start-daemon.sh.
#
# There is deliberately no default provider. Ceraa ships with no URL, model, or
# key baked in, so on first run it asks which provider to use and stores the
# answer per provider. Set these only if you want to pre-seed a provider from
# the environment instead of choosing in Telegram.

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Allowlisted Telegram user/chat ID
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_ID=

# Optional: pre-seed an OpenAI-compatible provider instead of using Telegram
# onboarding. Leave blank to choose a provider in Telegram.
CERAA_API_URL=
CERAA_MODEL=
CERAA_API_KEY=

# Where the bot should run
HOME=/home/assistant

# The Mini App surface.
#
# Off by default: set nothing and /web opens it on demand, which is the safer
# posture on a host nobody is watching. Set both of these to keep it up instead,
# and the trade is explicit — a port and a tunnel come up unattended at every
# boot, in front of an agent with bash and a credential store.
#
# Set both or neither. CERAA_MINIAPP=1 without the tunnel opens a loopback port
# nothing can reach, and CERAA_MINIAPP_TUNNEL=1 without the surface is ignored.
#
# Prefer on for a single-operator install. A quick tunnel is handed a new
# hostname every time it starts, so a surface that is only opened on demand leaves
# the menu button naming the hostname of a tunnel that died with the previous
# process, and tapping it answers Cloudflare 1033. The button is rewritten
# whenever an address is published, so nothing has to be re-entered by hand — but
# that only holds while something is actually running to rewrite it.
#
# BotFather's "Main App" is a different field, set only through BotFather, and
# this does not touch it. Leave it disabled unless the URL is one you control.
#
# Left commented on purpose. A token on its own is a complete install: /web opens
# the surface on demand and sets the menu button, with nothing to do in BotFather.
# Uncommenting only changes what happens after a restart.
# CERAA_MINIAPP=1
# CERAA_MINIAPP_TUNNEL=1
